WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:02.730 --> 00:00:03.580
- [Mark] Okay, Norman.

00:00:03.580 --> 00:00:05.850
- Hey, what's going on?

00:00:05.850 --> 00:00:06.683
- [Mark] Welcome back.

00:00:06.683 --> 00:00:08.100
- Yes sir, good to be back.

00:00:08.100 --> 00:00:10.751
- [Mark] So day after Thanksgiving,

00:00:10.751 --> 00:00:12.530
what's going on with you now?

00:00:12.530 --> 00:00:16.323
- Oh, well part-time workers
were laid off at the job.

00:00:17.510 --> 00:00:19.300
Usually that would be
something that would be

00:00:19.300 --> 00:00:20.883
a huge trigger for me.

00:00:22.210 --> 00:00:23.640
I would get in that mind frame

00:00:23.640 --> 00:00:25.170
always of I'll show them.

00:00:25.170 --> 00:00:26.400
- [Mark] So you got, you got laid off.

00:00:26.400 --> 00:00:30.660
- Yes, yes, I got laid off
along with about 12 others.

00:00:30.660 --> 00:00:32.750
We were all part-time workers.

00:00:32.750 --> 00:00:35.870
And you know, I understand
the onus of part-time.

00:00:35.870 --> 00:00:38.710
That's exactly what it
is, part-time, you know.

00:00:38.710 --> 00:00:40.893
We did a lot of work,
we did some overtime,

00:00:42.640 --> 00:00:43.930
but unfortunately, I mean this is

00:00:43.930 --> 00:00:46.171
what they decided due to COVID.

00:00:46.171 --> 00:00:48.630
It's not nothing that,
on me, so that's good.

00:00:48.630 --> 00:00:50.020
But usually I would
have that frame of mind

00:00:50.020 --> 00:00:52.323
with I'll show them and I go and fuck up.

00:00:53.260 --> 00:00:55.830
You know, and I've looked
back at those things

00:00:55.830 --> 00:00:57.680
and I'm like, okay, I didn't do that.

00:00:59.340 --> 00:01:00.940
Then I said, why didn't I do it?

00:01:02.890 --> 00:01:04.040
Well, I didn't want to.

00:01:05.340 --> 00:01:09.350
And then faced with

00:01:09.350 --> 00:01:11.113
what I would call a debacle.

00:01:12.380 --> 00:01:14.493
I stood up and I said, okay,

00:01:15.650 --> 00:01:18.010
let's go back to the drawing board.

00:01:18.010 --> 00:01:19.670
Go back and put your
resume back out there.

00:01:19.670 --> 00:01:20.503
- [Mark] Good for you.

00:01:20.503 --> 00:01:22.493
- And I have a interview Monday.

00:01:25.235 --> 00:01:26.260
- [Mark] That's great.

00:01:26.260 --> 00:01:27.110
You know, I mean,

00:01:29.240 --> 00:01:30.390
this is when life shows up.

00:01:30.390 --> 00:01:32.410
I mean, you know, just because you

00:01:32.410 --> 00:01:35.730
move away from something
that was bad for you

00:01:35.730 --> 00:01:38.940
doesn't mean that negative
things won't happen.

00:01:38.940 --> 00:01:40.100
You know, of course it's negative.

00:01:40.100 --> 00:01:41.650
You know, I loved the job.

00:01:41.650 --> 00:01:43.500
It was, it was a nice little commute.

00:01:44.425 --> 00:01:45.480
It was a wonderful job.

00:01:45.480 --> 00:01:47.030
You know, I was a floor leader,

00:01:48.271 --> 00:01:50.870
but you know unfortunately this is life,

00:01:50.870 --> 00:01:53.530
you know and this is what happens.

00:01:53.530 --> 00:01:55.340
So, you know, when life shows up

00:01:56.930 --> 00:02:00.273
for me, God better show up and show out.

00:02:02.870 --> 00:02:04.700
Or I'm going to show up
and I'm going to show out

00:02:04.700 --> 00:02:05.900
and I'm going to go out.

00:02:07.080 --> 00:02:08.850
You know, but I don't
do those things anymore.

00:02:08.850 --> 00:02:10.150
I do it one day at a time.

00:02:12.270 --> 00:02:14.258
Like I was telling my buddy the other day,

00:02:14.258 --> 00:02:15.380
I don't even count my days.

00:02:15.380 --> 00:02:17.370
You know, when I wake up in the morning,

00:02:17.370 --> 00:02:19.680
I go through my prayer meditation.

00:02:19.680 --> 00:02:21.970
I ask God what he wants me to do today.

00:02:21.970 --> 00:02:23.020
And I leave it alone.

00:02:23.990 --> 00:02:26.833
You know, as things
come, I deal with them.

00:02:28.770 --> 00:02:31.640
The holidays are usually something

00:02:31.640 --> 00:02:33.430
that kind of rattles me.

00:02:33.430 --> 00:02:35.530
Didn't rattle me this year

00:02:35.530 --> 00:02:39.020
because I really kind of got
the gist of thanksgiving.

00:02:39.020 --> 00:02:41.990
You know, thanks for God allowing me

00:02:41.990 --> 00:02:44.930
to be in His presence
and give me my life back.

00:02:44.930 --> 00:02:47.690
I'm thankful to the company for hiring me,

00:02:47.690 --> 00:02:49.710
at least giving me a chance.

00:02:49.710 --> 00:02:51.650
You know, you never
know who seen this video

00:02:51.650 --> 00:02:53.320
and said, oh hell no, we're
not going to hire him.

00:02:53.320 --> 00:02:54.310
He's a crack addict.

00:02:54.310 --> 00:02:55.440
You know, he's one check Norman,

00:02:55.440 --> 00:02:56.830
he always goes out, you know?

00:02:56.830 --> 00:02:59.310
Well I just dispelled that damn rumor.

00:02:59.310 --> 00:03:02.630
You know, I got a few checks,
and didn't go nowhere.

00:03:02.630 --> 00:03:06.040
Took care of some bills, took
care of some past due stuff,

00:03:06.040 --> 00:03:07.930
you know, don't have the money

00:03:07.930 --> 00:03:10.030
that I would want to have, but it's okay.

00:03:10.030 --> 00:03:10.910
You know, I'm breathing.

00:03:10.910 --> 00:03:12.640
I have something to eat.

00:03:12.640 --> 00:03:14.699
You know, it's a little tough right now,

00:03:14.699 --> 00:03:15.940
but it's going to be okay.

00:03:15.940 --> 00:03:17.040
It's going to be okay.

00:03:18.730 --> 00:03:21.620
When you really look at things

00:03:21.620 --> 00:03:24.313
in a frame of mind that it is what it is.

00:03:25.880 --> 00:03:28.300
It's like that power
of choice and control.

00:03:28.300 --> 00:03:31.210
I didn't have any power
over what they did.

00:03:31.210 --> 00:03:32.920
I really didn't have a choice

00:03:32.920 --> 00:03:34.810
and I had no control of the situation,

00:03:34.810 --> 00:03:37.823
but I did have control
over what I would do.

00:03:39.430 --> 00:03:42.563
I did have a semblance of
control of my thinking.

00:03:44.040 --> 00:03:47.233
Usually the first thought is pow.

00:03:48.980 --> 00:03:49.813
But it wasn't.

00:03:51.080 --> 00:03:53.943
And I thank God for that
because I said, okay,

00:03:55.330 --> 00:03:58.018
And I thought on the bus on the way home,

00:03:58.018 --> 00:04:00.670
I got to the house, I told my buddy,

00:04:00.670 --> 00:04:02.010
he was very encourage-able,

00:04:02.010 --> 00:04:05.580
as he always has been,
and as he always will be.

00:04:05.580 --> 00:04:08.450
He said, okay, well
you've never had a problem

00:04:08.450 --> 00:04:09.313
getting a job.

00:04:10.300 --> 00:04:12.480
You've had a problem keeping 'em.

00:04:12.480 --> 00:04:15.090
And guess what, this one was not on you.

00:04:15.090 --> 00:04:19.380
You didn't do anything to leave the job.

00:04:19.380 --> 00:04:22.140
You didn't do anything
to have the managers

00:04:22.140 --> 00:04:24.500
or anybody else saying
okay what's wrong with him

00:04:24.500 --> 00:04:26.250
or anything like that.

00:04:26.250 --> 00:04:29.930
It's just a normal
occurrence in everyday life.

00:04:29.930 --> 00:04:31.580
And you handled it.

00:04:31.580 --> 00:04:35.423
You know, you gotta have that wherewithal.

00:04:36.490 --> 00:04:38.940
- [Mark] how you handle
these setbacks, like this

00:04:39.920 --> 00:04:41.023
dictates so much of--
- Right.

00:04:41.023 --> 00:04:45.140
You know, it's just like, of
course I'm bummed out about it.

00:04:45.140 --> 00:04:48.860
You know because it was
a chance to go further.

00:04:48.860 --> 00:04:51.190
But I still have a chance to go further.

00:04:51.190 --> 00:04:53.093
As long as I have a chance,

00:04:54.940 --> 00:04:56.993
you take chances in life every day.

00:04:58.090 --> 00:04:59.650
Somebody had walked up to me one time

00:04:59.650 --> 00:05:02.240
and asked me did I want to gamble?

00:05:02.240 --> 00:05:03.410
I said, no, I'm already gambling.

00:05:03.410 --> 00:05:05.012
They said what do you mean?

00:05:05.012 --> 00:05:05.845
You're standing here talking to me.

00:05:05.845 --> 00:05:07.210
I gamble on life.

00:05:07.210 --> 00:05:08.700
Every time I took a hit of crack cocaine

00:05:08.700 --> 00:05:10.710
I was gambling with my life.

00:05:10.710 --> 00:05:12.870
Every time I did something
that I wasn't supposed to do

00:05:12.870 --> 00:05:14.020
I was gambling with my life.

00:05:14.020 --> 00:05:15.860
Especially taking something
from somebody else

00:05:15.860 --> 00:05:17.313
or something like that.

00:05:19.110 --> 00:05:20.590
You know, man, it is what it is.

00:05:20.590 --> 00:05:21.640
I'm gonna keep going.

00:05:26.460 --> 00:05:31.040
The humility that I'm
gaining from the experience

00:05:31.040 --> 00:05:36.040
of having a setback and not
going back is different.

00:05:39.100 --> 00:05:40.760
You know, I was thinking
this morning, I'm like,

00:05:40.760 --> 00:05:43.793
damn, man, you still going.

00:05:47.950 --> 00:05:51.463
They said, okay, bye-bye,
but you didn't say bye-bye.

00:05:52.300 --> 00:05:55.650
because I usually end the
book, this is the last chapter.

00:05:55.650 --> 00:05:57.500
And it's like four or five pages.

00:05:57.500 --> 00:06:00.740
There's no going on, there's
no trying to go to school

00:06:00.740 --> 00:06:03.540
and get a book report because
there is no book report.

00:06:03.540 --> 00:06:06.823
It's the same news all the
time, well, Norman's gone.

00:06:08.890 --> 00:06:12.160
I remember my son told me
one time he said he called me

00:06:12.160 --> 00:06:13.090
and he couldn't get ahold of me.

00:06:13.090 --> 00:06:14.440
He say, well, my dad's gone

00:06:15.950 --> 00:06:18.730
and I don't want him to say that anymore.

00:06:18.730 --> 00:06:20.850
You know he's a good kid.

00:06:20.850 --> 00:06:22.220
He's doing what he's supposed to do.

00:06:22.220 --> 00:06:24.720
He has a wonderful little
son, my little grandson.

00:06:26.321 --> 00:06:27.783
And he's doing what he's supposed to do.

00:06:30.202 --> 00:06:32.690
My middle daughter is in Las Vegas

00:06:32.690 --> 00:06:36.350
with my grandkids,
really miss my grandkids

00:06:36.350 --> 00:06:37.260
especially my granddaughters.

00:06:37.260 --> 00:06:39.110
Cause they, they like to
jump on me all the time

00:06:39.110 --> 00:06:40.270
and I'd like to pick them up,

00:06:40.270 --> 00:06:42.050
throw them on the couch
and they keep coming back.

00:06:42.050 --> 00:06:44.633
You know, I kind of dig that
kind of stuff, I'm a big kid.

00:06:46.310 --> 00:06:48.460
My oldest daughter is
doing extremely well.

00:06:49.450 --> 00:06:53.603
She's married, she lives in
Virginia and she's happy.

00:06:55.169 --> 00:06:58.660
And that's what really pushes me to

00:07:02.180 --> 00:07:04.830
those moments of blissfulness.

00:07:04.830 --> 00:07:07.470
You know, when I can just sit back

00:07:07.470 --> 00:07:08.680
recollect, just having a good day.

00:07:08.680 --> 00:07:10.030
And even sometimes when I would come home

00:07:10.030 --> 00:07:12.020
because I worked the night shift

00:07:12.020 --> 00:07:16.160
and I'd come home about
7:15 watching the news

00:07:16.160 --> 00:07:19.550
I'll eat something and I'll
sit back and I'll think,

00:07:19.550 --> 00:07:22.163
you know, hey, how did your day go?

00:07:23.260 --> 00:07:25.790
Do you, did you keep something to yourself

00:07:25.790 --> 00:07:28.073
which you should have
shared with somebody else?

00:07:30.370 --> 00:07:32.703
What could you do better for the next day?

00:07:33.550 --> 00:07:34.670
And that's how I look at it.

00:07:34.670 --> 00:07:36.093
You know, I don't have any,

00:07:37.360 --> 00:07:41.260
it's not so much that getting
high is not an option anymore

00:07:43.170 --> 00:07:45.533
because you always have
choices and options.

00:07:48.380 --> 00:07:50.680
It's just not a risk
that I'm willing to take.

00:07:53.840 --> 00:07:55.800
To have all of these people who

00:07:55.800 --> 00:07:58.093
give me so much encouragement, you know

00:07:58.093 --> 00:08:01.530
I still go in there and I'll
read them over and over again.

00:08:01.530 --> 00:08:04.230
And most importantly, the naysayers.

00:08:04.230 --> 00:08:06.913
You boost me, so keep
those bad comments coming.

00:08:08.730 --> 00:08:11.940
Like LeBron says, I want my damn respect

00:08:11.940 --> 00:08:16.770
but respect is earned and I
don't owe anyone, anything.

00:08:16.770 --> 00:08:18.670
And you guys out there that are listening

00:08:18.670 --> 00:08:19.970
you don't owe me anything.

00:08:21.300 --> 00:08:23.150
But to the naysayers,
keep the comments coming,

00:08:23.150 --> 00:08:24.490
cause they really boost me.

00:08:24.490 --> 00:08:27.390
It's like, I'm a space X,
rocket, and I'm always going up.

00:08:29.089 --> 00:08:30.840
You know, I'm even gonna
stop commenting back

00:08:30.840 --> 00:08:32.040
because I don't need to.

00:08:33.210 --> 00:08:34.510
My action will speak so loud

00:08:34.510 --> 00:08:36.890
you can't hear shit I'm saying.

00:08:36.890 --> 00:08:38.340
That's how I'm looking at it.

00:08:39.410 --> 00:08:40.910
- [Mark] You seem a much
more grounded this time

00:08:40.910 --> 00:08:42.030
than any other time I've seen.

00:08:42.030 --> 00:08:43.280
- Yeah. I mean, you know,

00:08:45.340 --> 00:08:49.650
well the seed is planted
and it's being watered.

00:08:49.650 --> 00:08:50.840
Now, it's just not going to sprout up

00:08:50.840 --> 00:08:54.340
and turn into a Sequoia tree overnight.

00:08:54.340 --> 00:08:55.840
I mean, this is an ongoing process.

00:08:55.840 --> 00:08:58.230
You're looking at a person who's used

00:08:58.230 --> 00:08:59.793
for 30 something years.

00:09:01.440 --> 00:09:02.760
Was an active user at a job.

00:09:02.760 --> 00:09:04.573
Nobody knew what the hell I was doing.

00:09:07.797 --> 00:09:09.700
It's just, the choice is up to me.

00:09:09.700 --> 00:09:11.823
You know, I faced those times,

00:09:13.840 --> 00:09:14.980
actually to tell you the truth,

00:09:14.980 --> 00:09:17.383
and I don't want to sound
arrogant or egotistical,

00:09:19.110 --> 00:09:23.320
I welcome the times that will come

00:09:24.170 --> 00:09:27.093
where I'm faced with a decision.

00:09:28.820 --> 00:09:32.110
Because usually I only had one decision

00:09:33.760 --> 00:09:36.393
now, not so much do I have a decision,

00:09:36.393 --> 00:09:37.823
I have choices I can make.

00:09:38.710 --> 00:09:41.041
I can choose to go the wrong way.

00:09:41.041 --> 00:09:42.570
I can choose to go the right way,

00:09:42.570 --> 00:09:44.065
I can keep going forward.

00:09:44.065 --> 00:09:45.765
Or I could choose to go backwards.

00:09:49.737 --> 00:09:51.087
And the choice is up to me.

00:09:52.370 --> 00:09:55.680
So we just keep going, we
take it one day at a time.

00:09:55.680 --> 00:09:56.780
We don't look further.

00:09:58.250 --> 00:10:00.050
I'm prepared for the interview Monday

00:10:00.050 --> 00:10:01.250
even though it's Friday.

00:10:02.260 --> 00:10:04.193
The game face will be on Sunday.

00:10:05.800 --> 00:10:08.173
The Mamba Mentality will be there Monday.

00:10:10.630 --> 00:10:14.993
I don't know if anybody ever
really listened to Kobe Bryant.

00:10:17.260 --> 00:10:21.090
But for me and going through
what I've been going through

00:10:22.930 --> 00:10:27.190
he's helped me tremendously
in what he said about himself.

00:10:27.190 --> 00:10:30.950
And how he had instituted wherewithal

00:10:32.820 --> 00:10:35.393
because he said he wanted to be the best.

00:10:36.880 --> 00:10:37.943
So he worked at it.

00:10:39.840 --> 00:10:44.623
So if I want to be better,
I need to work at it.

00:10:46.240 --> 00:10:50.270
Day, after day, after day,
every day is not going to be

00:10:50.270 --> 00:10:53.660
like it is outside
sunny, clear blue skies.

00:10:53.660 --> 00:10:55.490
There gonna be some clouds.

00:10:55.490 --> 00:10:57.020
There gonna be some rain.

00:10:57.020 --> 00:10:58.820
There's gonna be some thunderstorms.

00:11:01.180 --> 00:11:02.710
Am I going to carry that umbrella

00:11:02.710 --> 00:11:04.610
of wherewithal with me at all times.

00:11:04.610 --> 00:11:07.490
That is the key question right now.

00:11:07.490 --> 00:11:10.983
Of course, because
that's what I want to do.

00:11:12.060 --> 00:11:14.363
I don't owe my kids anything.

00:11:16.550 --> 00:11:18.700
But what I want them to know

00:11:18.700 --> 00:11:21.280
is that I'm going to do the
best that I possibly can

00:11:21.280 --> 00:11:22.573
to not so much, see any,

00:11:23.950 --> 00:11:25.480
any male could be called daddy

00:11:25.480 --> 00:11:27.333
but it takes a man to be a father.

00:11:28.460 --> 00:11:30.480
I have to relearn how to be a father

00:11:31.869 --> 00:11:33.319
because I never had a father.

00:11:35.040 --> 00:11:36.373
So I'm relearning that.

00:11:38.066 --> 00:11:42.300
I'm really learning how to handle setbacks

00:11:42.300 --> 00:11:45.970
and negative situations
in a conducive manner

00:11:45.970 --> 00:11:47.403
rather than running.

00:11:49.130 --> 00:11:51.210
I mean these 56 year old legs,

00:11:51.210 --> 00:11:52.440
they still got some pump in them,

00:11:52.440 --> 00:11:55.263
but I'm tired, tired of running.

00:11:56.415 --> 00:11:58.360
And we're just going to
take it a day at a time.

00:11:58.360 --> 00:12:02.243
It's all we can do, you know,
it's either this or that.

00:12:03.780 --> 00:12:04.653
Choice is mine.

00:12:07.470 --> 00:12:09.880
- [Mark] Excellent, you're doing it, man.

00:12:09.880 --> 00:12:11.049
I can tell.

00:12:11.049 --> 00:12:11.882
- I'm just going to keep going.

00:12:11.882 --> 00:12:13.965
- [Mark] Yeah, you don't even seem like

00:12:13.965 --> 00:12:15.450
(laughing)

00:12:15.450 --> 00:12:18.300
- He looks at me like, man, you know,

00:12:18.300 --> 00:12:19.900
you don't really look like Norman no more.

00:12:19.900 --> 00:12:21.080
- No you don't.
- What the fuck you mean

00:12:21.080 --> 00:12:22.565
I don't look like Norman?

00:12:22.565 --> 00:12:23.398
- [Mark] Not the Norman that we've known.

00:12:23.398 --> 00:12:25.981
- He said because you was a
bony motherfucker, that's why.

00:12:25.981 --> 00:12:28.310
I was like, well, you know, hey, you know?

00:12:28.310 --> 00:12:31.530
Cause I wanted to cut
my hair, but you know

00:12:31.530 --> 00:12:33.420
didn't have the money to do it.

00:12:33.420 --> 00:12:34.470
And you know, because I had
to take care of some things

00:12:34.470 --> 00:12:35.370
but I'm glad that,

00:12:36.526 --> 00:12:38.360
see the records of your past will come up

00:12:38.360 --> 00:12:41.720
a lot, especially when you get sober.

00:12:41.720 --> 00:12:43.200
Because you've done some things

00:12:43.200 --> 00:12:45.380
under the auspices of getting high.

00:12:45.380 --> 00:12:48.160
And then when you get
sober, here they come.

00:12:48.160 --> 00:12:50.950
I.e. bills, collectors, things like that.

00:12:50.950 --> 00:12:53.010
I have some negative
things on my credit report.

00:12:53.010 --> 00:12:54.130
I took care of them.

